    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "source": "In the Fong and Saunders case, this value holds an estimate of the relative error in the data defining the matrix *A*.",
      "ko": "This method plays the available media data at the specified `rate` regardless of whether there is sufficient media buffered to ensure smooth playback.",
      "sourceHash": "69247c71944c51334c03e31a8a8a302b0db15c44f7aa4b8e192ece7d0bfa1118",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0002",
      "source": "For example, if *A* is accurate to about six digits, set [`atol`](sparselsmroptions/atol.md) `= 1.0e-6`.",
      "ko": "If media data exists in the playback buffer, calling this method changes the player’s playback rate to the specified `rate` and its [`timeControlStatus`](avplayer/timecontrolstatus-swift.property.md) to a value of [`AVPlayer.TimeControlStatus.playing`](avplayer/timecontrolstatus-swift.enum/playing.md).",
      "sourceHash": "2dc5e2b09d448651660f0f8a07018eafd25331e482b7012ccc52c28d7e5cd753",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
